# Nebula UI v3

Full brief: **`CURSOR-HANDOFF.md`** at the repo root. Read it before the first edit to
`obsauto/gui.py`. Code facts live in `CLAUDE.md`.

## Authority order

```
design/ui-v3/BUILD-SPEC.md  >  design/ui-v3/FRAMES.md (and the .dc.html)  >  everything else
```

The mockup says so itself: *"If a frame and this table disagree, this table wins."*

`design/ui-v3/_ds/nocturne-*/styles.css` is the **house** design system. **v3 does not use
it** — the mockup overrides it wholesale. Never link it; never take a token from it.
Use `obsauto/design_v3.py`, which is § 05 of the spec as code.

## Five things that will bite you

1. **Never animate the `tk.Canvas` per-frame.** Any canvas change forces a *full window*
   composite — ~100ms, and the cost is **flat**, independent of how much changed. A 12fps
   decorative timer measured **p50 110ms at 95% CPU**; removing all of it gave 16ms at 4%.
   So the spec's aurora drift, star drift, pointer spotlight and pointer lean are **not
   implementable as written**. Render them **once at launch with a random seed** into the
   static backdrop instead — that keeps "randomised per launch, no two sessions alike"
   and costs nothing. `tests/test_frame_pacing.py` fails if a per-frame timer returns.

2. **No fabricated data.** Every number in the frames is mockup filler. If a value has no
   real source, **build the source or omit the element** — never ship a plausible
   placeholder or a `0` that means "not implemented". Macropad has **no HID layer at all**;
   it stays honestly empty until one exists. (This is why v2 dropped Mark clip, the search
   pill and the res/fps chips.)

3. **Never call `obs.connect()` on the Tk thread** — it blocks up to 5s, and at startup that
   is the normal case. Worker thread, marshal back through `_ui()`.

4. **`except X as e` unbinds `e` when the block exits.** Any `lambda` capturing it that runs
   later via `after()`/`_ui()` dies with `NameError`. Bind to a plain local first. Under
   `pythonw` this crash is **silent** — stderr doesn't exist — which is why
   `report_callback_exception` routes to the app log. Don't remove that.

5. **Keep the caches and the coalescing.** `_regen_glass()` is ~35ms a call and re-runs on
   every state change. `_log` only appends to a locked buffer; `_flush_log` batches the
   textbox write on the Tk thread (a per-line write is one composite each — a burst pegged
   the UI at 371ms).

## Two open decisions (don't guess — see CURSOR-HANDOFF.md §2.1, §2.4)

- **Background:** static randomised render (recommended) vs. animated. See rule 1.
- **Window:** keep the fixed-pixel `ScaledCanvas` design at 1280×808 (recommended) vs.
  make the content pane reflow to honour the 1080×700 minimum.

## Build order — from the spec, follow it

1. Chassis (tray, core, titlebar, rail, empty pane) until it matches frame **2a** exactly.
2. Hero card + its 4 states driven by **one state enum** (recording / watching / paused /
   disconnected). Then stat tiles, then activity log.
3. Tray + window chrome — `−` and `×` both hide, **Quit only in the tray menu**.
4. Single-slot toast — **build the replace-in-place path before the visuals**.
5. Clips pane.
6. Settings — the mono config-key labels under each field **are part of the design**.
   Write on blur, not per keystroke. Merge over `DEFAULTS`; never drop an unknown key.
7. Games, Macropad, mini overlay last. Mini overlay **never shows while idle**.

## Non-negotiable visual invariants

- Palette is **Nebula Deep only** (`design_v3.COLORS`). No emoji, no gradient floods,
  no second accent hue. **Ember `#FF5C7A` is live-and-errors only.**
- **Every card is two layers** — tinted outer shell, darker inner core. A flat card is a bug.
- Hairlines are `rgba(245,243,255, .055–.09)`, never solid grey. Rules **fade at both ends
  over 32–48px**.
- Panels over the backdrop sit at **72–92% opacity** — a fully opaque panel is a bug.
- Icons: Phosphor **Light** at 12–24px. The only Fill glyphs are `ph-circle` (status dots,
  6–8px) and `ph-square` (stop, 9–11px).
- The elapsed timer ticks **once per second**, tabular figures, fixed width, and must not
  reflow its neighbours.

